It looks like there might be a slight mix-up! Social Security Numbers (SSNs) do not have expiration dates. 

If you are applying for a six-month visa, the expiration date requirement usually applies to your **passport**. Most countries require your passport to be valid for at least six months *beyond* your planned date of departure from their country. 

I highly recommend checking the specific visa requirements for your destination country regarding passport validity. If your passport is expiring soon, you may need to renew it before applying for the visa.

